{"name":"Mangrove","hex":"#757461","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mangrove","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various tropical and subtropical evergreen shrubs or trees chiefly of the Rhizophoraceae family that have aerial roots and grow in clumps in brackish intertidal coastal areas;  any of various trees of the genus Rhizophora, especially the red mangrove (Rhizophora mangle). .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A forest of such shrubs or trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mangrove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mangrove","blocks":[{"text":"A mangrove is a shrub or tree that grows mainly in coastal saline or brackish water. Mangroves grow in an equatorial climate, typically along coastlines and tidal rivers. They have particular adaptations to take in extra oxygen and remove salt, allowing them to tolerate conditions that kill most plants. The term is also used for tropical coastal vegetation consisting of such species. Mangroves are taxonomically diverse due to convergent evolution in several plant families. They occur worldwide in tropical and subtropical coastal areas, mainly between latitudes 30° N and 30° S, with the greatest mangrove area within 5° of the equator. Mangrove plant families first appeared during the Late Cretaceous to Paleocene epochs and became widely distributed in part due to the movement of tectonic plates. The oldest known fossils of mangrove palm date to 75 million years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Sonneratia_alba_-_Manado_%282%29.JPG/330px-Sonneratia_alba_-_Manado_%282%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mangrove","wikidata":"Q19756"},{"title":"Mangrove (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Mangrove is a 2020 historical legal drama film directed by British director Steve McQueen and co-written by McQueen and Alastair Siddons, about the Mangrove restaurant in west London and the 1971 trial of the Mangrove Nine. It stars Letitia Wright, Shaun Parkes, Malachi Kirby, Rochenda Sandall, Alex Jennings and Jack Lowden."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0c/Poster_for_2020_film_Mangrove.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mangrove_(film)","wikidata":"Q103404063"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Mangrove_roots_at_low_tide.jpg/500px-Mangrove_roots_at_low_tide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Mangrove_roots_at_low_tide.jpg/1280px-Mangrove_roots_at_low_tide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Mangrove_roots_at_low_tide.jpg/500px-Mangrove_roots_at_low_tide.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mangrove roots at low tide in the Philippines","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMangrove_roots_at_low_tide.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Mangroves_in_Kannur%2C_India.jpg/500px-Mangroves_in_Kannur%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Mangroves_in_Kannur%2C_India.jpg/500px-Mangroves_in_Kannur%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mangroves are adapted to saline conditions","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMangroves_in_Kannur%2C_India.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Mangrove_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Mangrove_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Mangrove_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Mangrove_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red mangrove","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMangrove_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Saltcrystals_on_avicennia_marina_var_resinifera_leaves.JPG/500px-Saltcrystals_on_avicennia_marina_var_resinifera_leaves.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Saltcrystals_on_avicennia_marina_var_resinifera_leaves.JPG/500px-Saltcrystals_on_avicennia_marina_var_resinifera_leaves.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Salt crystals formed on an Avicennia marina leaf","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaltcrystals_on_avicennia_marina_var_resinifera_leaves.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Pneumatophore_overkill_-_grey_mangrove.JPG/330px-Pneumatophore_overkill_-_grey_mangrove.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Pneumatophore_overkill_-_grey_mangrove.JPG/960px-Pneumatophore_overkill_-_grey_mangrove.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Pneumatophore_overkill_-_grey_mangrove.JPG/330px-Pneumatophore_overkill_-_grey_mangrove.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APneumatophore_overkill_-_grey_mangrove.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Plody_mangrovnika_%28Rhizophora_mangle%29.jpg/250px-Plody_mangrovnika_%28Rhizophora_mangle%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Plody_mangrovnika_%28Rhizophora_mangle%29.jpg/500px-Plody_mangrovnika_%28Rhizophora_mangle%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Plody_mangrovnika_%28Rhizophora_mangle%29.jpg/250px-Plody_mangrovnika_%28Rhizophora_mangle%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlody_mangrovnika_(Rhizophora_mangle).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Water_filtration_in_mangrove_roots.webp/500px-Water_filtration_in_mangrove_roots.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Water_filtration_in_mangrove_roots.webp/1280px-Water_filtration_in_mangrove_roots.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Water_filtration_in_mangrove_roots.webp/500px-Water_filtration_in_mangrove_roots.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Seawater filtration in the root of the mangrove Rhizophora stylosa. (a) Schematic of the root. The outermost layer is composed of three layers. The root is immersed in NaCl solution. (b) Water passes through the outermost layer when a negative suction pressure is applied across the outermost layer. The Donnan potential effect repels Cl− ions from the first sublayer of the outermost layer. Na+ ions attach to the first layer to satisfy the electro-neutrality requirement and salt retention eventually occurs.[27]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_filtration_in_mangrove_roots.webp"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/One_week_old_Mangarove%2C_Qatif%2C_Saudi_Arabia%2C_Late_August_2020_2_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-One_week_old_Mangarove%2C_Qatif%2C_Saudi_Arabia%2C_Late_August_2020_2_%28cropped%29.jp